Sipho runs a fruit and vegetable stall in Mbare market, Harare. His capital at 1 January 2025 was US\$18,740. During 2025:

- he paid US\$2,500 from a family gift into the business bank account;
- he withdrew US\$6,300 in cash for personal use;
- he took fruit costing US\$540 for his household;
- the business paid US\$380 for his daughter's school trip.

His draft profit for the year, calculated before taking account of the goods and the school trip, was US\$10,095. The school trip had been debited to general expenses; the goods taken had not been recorded.
